(property "Description" " | design | Bourns MF-MSMF075/24-2 ahead of the fan switch Q304 (W2 CTRL-5, review RV4-E-5): LAB5 -> F301 -> E3_FAN5 -> Q304 -> E3_FAN5_P, so a short of the node between the PTC and the switch, of the switch or of the fan side is limited by the PTC and never by F102 4 A alone. Ihold 0.75 A / Itrip 1.50 A at 23 C, Ihold 1.01 A at -20 C, 0.49 A at 70 C; 8.0 A trips in 0.2 s max; Rmin 0.11 ohm, R1max 0.45 ohm; Imax 40 A at 24 V (Bourns MF-MSMF REV. BE 09/26, https://www.bourns.com/docs/Product-Datasheets/mf-msmf.pdf, read 2026-11-13). It limits the Noctua lead S27 (1x26 AWG) instead of F102 4 A; the flyback D305 and C318/C319 stay across the fan after the switch (R-E3-17).; Reflow soldering: wave soldering only with the device on the top side opposite the heat source, hand soldering not recommended (Bourns MF-MSMF REV. BE 09/26, solder reflow recommendations, read 2026-11-13); F301 sits on the bottom side of CTRL, so it goes through the bottom reflow pass." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
