(property "Description" " | design | W2 CTRL-5 (review RV4-E-5): the PTC F301 sits ahead of Q304 (source on E3_FAN5 behind the PTC, drain on E3_FAN5_P); the gate pull-up R367 stays on LAB5, so with Q303 off VGS >= 0 V and the switch stays off also when the PTC drops voltage. AO3401A Rev 3.1 (Dec 2023, read 2026-11-13): ID -4.0 A at 25 C / -3.2 A at 70 C, IDM -27 A, RDS(on) < 60 mOhm at VGS -4.5 V, RthJA 100 C/W (125 C/W max, steady state). In the old order a short of the node between Q304 and the PTC drew F102 current through Q304: the MINI 0297004 fuse carries 110 % for 360000 s and opens 135 % only in 0.75 -600 s (Littelfuse MINI 32 V data sheet), about 1.2-1.7 W in SOT-23 (MODEL), over TJ 150 C." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
