(property "Description" "Pullup on the GPIO side of gate series resistor: powered Pico reset/highimpedance asserts MCPreset; normal firmware actively sinks GP17 low to release it. | design | About3.3mA static current is sunk by GP17 in normal release state. R393 has no static voltage-divider drop when GP17 actively low because the pullup is on its GPIO side.; The1k pullup overrides weak RP2040 pad pulldowns during reset. Verify gate high and RESETlow over actual supply ramp, brownout andtemperature." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
